## Non-visual contracts that the rewrite must preserve

These behaviors are enforced by server code and must remain unchanged unless a
separate architecture decision (ADR) explicitly says otherwise. The rewrite
targets visual structure and interactive behavior, not the security surface.

### Menu visibility — `src/lib/server/utils/admin-pages.ts`
- `ADMIN_PAGE_DEFS` is the single source of truth for every admin page.
- `getAuthorizedAdminPages(user)` (line 135 of `admin-rbac.ts`) resolves menu
  visibility from `ADMIN_CONFIG` + `MODULES` + stored role permissions.
- A page disabled in `ADMIN_CONFIG` or with its module `MODULES[module].enabled
  === false` is excluded from both the menu AND the page gate (404).

### Page access — `src/lib/server/utils/admin-rbac.ts`
- `requireAdminPage(event, pageId)` (line 114) gates every admin route:
  1. authentication required (401)
  2. page enabled in config (404)
  3. user's role in the page's configured role list (403)
  4. stored role permissions (`roles.permissions` JSON) must not deny (403)
- Custom roles (not in the config role lists) are authorized ONLY when their
  stored permissions explicitly allow the page.

### Page enablement — `src/project/site-config.ts`
- `ADMIN_CONFIG.system[pageId].enabled` / `ADMIN_CONFIG.websiteModules[key].enabled`
  control whether a page exists. A disabled page returns 404 from
  `requireAdminPage` and never appears in the menu.
- `MODULES[key].enabled` controls website-content modules independently from admin.

### Forced password change — `src/routes/admin/+layout.server.ts`
- `event.locals.user.mustChangePassword` (line 65) redirects every
  authenticated admin request to `/admin/change-password` until the bootstrap
  credential is replaced. The `/admin/change-password` page itself is exempt
  (line 56). `requireAdminPage` also enforces this (line 102 of admin-rbac.ts).

### Layout-provided CSRF token — `src/routes/admin/+layout.server.ts`
- `event.cookies.get(CSRF_COOKIE_NAME)` (line 73) renders the CSRF token into
  page data so plain form submissions (no JS, or before hydration) carry a
  valid `_csrf` value. The rewrite must not remove this.

### Unread contact count — `src/routes/admin/+layout.server.ts`
- `getCachedUnreadCount()` (line 43) with a 10-second TTL serves the unread
  badge. The rewrite must preserve the existing badge on the contacts icon.

### Verification table

| Role | Menu visibility | Route access | Mutation access (system keys) |
|---|---|---|---|
| master | All enabled pages | All enabled pages | Allowed (system + content) |
| admin | All enabled pages | All enabled pages | Allowed (system + content) |
| editor | Content-module pages (blog, faq, features, testimonials); dashboard; translations (content only toggle) | Content-module pages + dashboard + translations | Content keys only; system keys rejected (403) |
| Disabled modules | Page hidden from menu | 404 from `requireAdminPage` | N/A |
| `mustChangePassword=1` | Menu hidden (redirected) | Redirect to `/admin/change-password` | Mutations blocked (`requireAdminPage` → 403 via `assertPasswordChanged`) |

---

## Server-side system-translation authorization

### ✅ Implemented: `src/lib/server/services/translations.ts`

The shared guard `isSystemKey(key)` classifies keys by prefix using the same
`SYSTEM_PREFIXES` (`admin.`, `nav.`, `common.`, `auth.`, `validation.`,
`footer.`, `error.`, `apiErrors.`) that `classifyTranslationType` uses. One
source of truth for classification.

Every translation mutation endpoint now enforces the guard:

| Endpoint | Guard applied |
|---|---|
| `POST /api/admin/translations` | `isSystemKey(key)` → 403 unless master/admin |
| `POST /api/admin/translations/batch` | `isSystemKey(key)` → 403 unless master/admin |
| `PUT /api/admin/translations/[locale]` | `isSystemKey(key)` → skip (not 403, so bulk updates still save content keys) |
| `DELETE /api/admin/translations/[locale]` | `isSystemKey(key)` → 403 unless master/admin |
| `PUT /api/admin/translations/[locale]/[key]` | `isSystemKey(key)` → 403 unless master/admin |
| `DELETE /api/admin/translations/[locale]/[key]` | `isSystemKey(key)` → 403 unless master/admin |

The UI restrictions in `src/routes/admin/translations/+page.svelte` (lock icon,
disabled edit/delete for editor role on system keys) are a **convenience
layer** — the real security boundary is the API guard above. The UI and API
both classify keys via the same `isSystemKey` / `classifyTranslationType`
function, exported from `src/lib/server/services/translations.ts`.

